# G14 — the source-normalization decision, computed

**The Riemann Hypothesis is not proved.**  Nothing was weakened and nothing was
assumed: `RiemannHypothesisFor`, `RiemannHypothesis` and every earlier statement
are untouched; there is no `sorry`/`admit`, no `axiom`, no postulate, no Boolean
receipt, no numerical evidence and no `@[implemented_by]` in any Lean source of
this cycle.  `lake build RiemannAnalytic` succeeds (8098 jobs) and
`#print axioms` on every new theorem returns only
`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`.

The instruction for this cycle was: *stop improving the prime estimate;
substitute the actual definitions and compute the source normalization ratio;
and run the deterministic log-frequency pigeonhole experiment.*  Both were done,
and both produced definite answers.

